<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani bourse adjusts trading hours for Ramadan.</title>
<headline>Pakistani bourse adjusts trading hours for Ramadan.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading at the Karachi Stock Exchange will start at 10.00 a.m. (0500 GMT) and close at 1.00 p.m. (0800 GMT) during the Moslem fasting month of Ramadan, dealers said on Sunday.</p>
<p>Trading hours are normally from 10.15 a.m. (0515 GMT) to 2.00 p.m. (0900 GMT).</p>
<p>Ramadan ends around February 10.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
